# Allowlist: the image is built from the package and the web assets it serves, nothing
# else. In particular no .env, no captures, downloads or CA material, no .venv, no .git.
*
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!wx_dlh/
!web/inject.js
!web/dashboard.html
!web/dashboard.js
!scripts/docker-entrypoint.sh
# Docker takes the last matching pattern, so these come after the negations: `*` only
# matches the top level, so `!wx_dlh/` would otherwise re-include a CA dir, a key or an
# .env someone put below it (`--ca-dir wx_dlh/ca`, say).
**/__pycache__
**/.env*
**/*.pem
**/*.cer
**/*.crt
**/*.key
**/*.p12
